  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "session-setup-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🛠️ Example 1: Developer Experience - Quick Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"From zero to semantic AI in 30 seconds\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Setting up Fenic is dead simple. One session configuration gives you access to all semantic operations across multiple LLM providers. No complex initialization, no boilerplate code - just pure productivity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "session-setup",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import fenic as fc\n",
    "from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n",
    "from typing import List, Optional\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# ⚡ One configuration for all semantic operations\n",
    "config = fc.SessionConfig(\n",
    "    app_name=\"fenic_in_120_seconds\",\n",
    "    semantic=fc.SemanticConfig(\n",
    "        language_models={\n",
    "            \"fast\": fc.OpenAILanguageModel(\n",
    "                model_name=\"gpt-4o-mini\",  # Fast and cost-effective\n",
    "                rpm=500,\n",
    "                tpm=200_000\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "            \"powerful\": fc.OpenAILanguageModel(\n",
    "                model_name=\"gpt-4o\",  # More capable for complex tasks\n",
    "                rpm=100,\n",
    "                tpm=50_000\n",
    "            )\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🚀 Start your Fenic session\n",
    "session = fc.Session.get_or_create(config)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Fenic session ready!\")\n",
    "print(\"🧠 Available models:\", list(config.semantic.language_models.keys()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "classification-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🎯 Example 2: Core Capability - Effortless Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"How many lines of code does it take to classify messy text? Less than 10.\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Traditional text classification requires training models, managing datasets, and complex preprocessing. With Fenic, you just describe your categories and let the LLM handle the rest. Perfect for support tickets, user feedback, or any text categorization task."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "classification",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📝 Sample customer support tickets (the messy, real-world kind)\n",
    "support_tickets = [\n",
    "    {\"ticket_id\": \"T001\", \"content\": \"I can't log into my account at all. Keep getting 'invalid password' even though I'm sure it's correct. This is really frustrating!\"},\n",
    "    {\"ticket_id\": \"T002\", \"content\": \"Hey, just wanted to say your app is amazing! The new dark mode feature is exactly what I needed. Keep up the great work!\"},\n",
    "    {\"ticket_id\": \"T003\", \"content\": \"The payment went through but I never received my premium subscription. It's been 3 days now. Can you please help?\"},\n",
    "    {\"ticket_id\": \"T004\", \"content\": \"Feature request: Would love to see integration with Google Calendar. That would make this app perfect for my workflow.\"},\n",
    "    {\"ticket_id\": \"T005\", \"content\": \"App keeps crashing when I try to export data. Happens every single time on iOS 17.2. Please fix this ASAP.\"},\n",
    "    {\"ticket_id\": \"T006\", \"content\": \"Thanks for the quick response to my last issue. Your support team is fantastic and really helped solve my problem!\"},\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🚀 Create DataFrame and classify in one line\n",
    "df = session.create_dataframe(support_tickets)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🎯 Classify tickets into categories (this is where the magic happens)\n",
    "classified_df = df.select(\n",
    "    \"ticket_id\",\n",
    "    \"content\", \n",
    "    fc.semantic.classify(\n",
    "        \"content\", \n",
    "        [\"bug_report\", \"feature_request\", \"billing_issue\", \"praise\", \"login_problem\"]\n",
    "    ).alias(\"category\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🎯 Automatic Classification Results:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "classified_df.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📊 Quick category breakdown\n",
    "print(\"\\n📊 Category Distribution:\")\n",
    "category_stats = classified_df.group_by(\"category\").agg(fc.builtin.count(\"*\").alias(\"count\"))\n",
    "category_stats.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "extraction-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🔍 Example 3: Core Capability - Semantic Extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"Turn unstructured text into structured data instantly\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine extracting structured information from messy text without writing complex regex patterns or rules. Fenic uses Pydantic schemas to ensure the LLM returns exactly the structure you need, with built-in validation and type safety."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "extraction",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📋 Define what you want to extract using Pydantic\n",
    "class PersonInfo(BaseModel):\n",
    "    name: str = Field(description=\"Full name of the person\")\n",
    "    age: Optional[int] = Field(description=\"Age in years, if mentioned\")\n",
    "    occupation: Optional[str] = Field(description=\"Job or profession\")\n",
    "    location: Optional[str] = Field(description=\"City, state, or country\")\n",
    "    interests: List[str] = Field(description=\"Hobbies or interests mentioned\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📝 Unstructured text bios (like you'd find on social media)\n",
    "user_bios = [\n",
    "    {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"bio\": \"Sarah Chen, 28, software engineer living in San Francisco. Love hiking, photography, and making sourdough bread on weekends!\"},\n",
    "    {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"bio\": \"Just a dad from Austin trying to balance work and family. Into BBQ, guitar playing, and coaching little league baseball.\"},\n",
    "    {\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"bio\": \"Dr. Maria Rodriguez - pediatrician in Miami. Passionate about salsa dancing, medical research, and traveling to new countries.\"},\n",
    "    {\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"bio\": \"Tokyo-based artist and designer. 35 years old. Creating digital art, collecting vintage vinyl, and exploring Japan's mountains.\"},\n",
    "    {\"user_id\": \"U005\", \"bio\": \"College student studying computer science. Love gaming, anime, coding side projects, and bubble tea adventures in Seattle.\"},\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_bios = session.create_dataframe(user_bios)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🔍 Extract structured data using your schema\n",
    "extracted_df = df_bios.select(\n",
    "    \"user_id\",\n",
    "    fc.semantic.extract(\n",
    "        \"bio\",\n",
    "        PersonInfo,  # Your Pydantic schema defines the structure\n",
    "        model_alias=\"fast\"  # Use the fast model for simple extraction\n",
    "    ).alias(\"person_info\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📊 Display extracted structured data\n",
    "structured_df = extracted_df.select(\n",
    "    \"user_id\",\n",
    "    extracted_df.person_info.name.alias(\"name\"),\n",
    "    extracted_df.person_info.age.alias(\"age\"),\n",
    "    extracted_df.person_info.occupation.alias(\"occupation\"),\n",
    "    extracted_df.person_info.location.alias(\"location\"),\n",
    "    extracted_df.person_info.interests.alias(\"interests\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🔍 Structured Extraction Results:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "structured_df.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "semantic-joins-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🔗 Example 4: Core Capability - Semantic Joins\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"What if SQL joins understood language instead of exact strings?\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Traditional joins require exact matches. Semantic joins understand that \"NYC\" means \"New York City\" and \"SF\" means \"San Francisco\". This is revolutionary for messy real-world data where the same entity appears in different formats."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "semantic-joins",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 🏢 Company data with inconsistent city naming\n",
    "companies = [\n",
    "    {\"company\": \"TechCorp\", \"location\": \"San Francisco\", \"employees\": 1200},\n",
    "    {\"company\": \"DataFlow\", \"location\": \"NYC\", \"employees\": 800},\n",
    "    {\"company\": \"CloudWorks\", \"location\": \"Seattle\", \"employees\": 650},\n",
    "    {\"company\": \"AI Dynamics\", \"location\": \"The Big Apple\", \"employees\": 450},\n",
    "    {\"company\": \"StartupX\", \"location\": \"SF Bay Area\", \"employees\": 120}\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🌡️ Weather data with official city names\n",
    "weather_data = [\n",
    "    {\"city\": \"San Francisco\", \"temperature\": 68, \"condition\": \"Foggy\"},\n",
    "    {\"city\": \"New York City\", \"temperature\": 72, \"condition\": \"Sunny\"},\n",
    "    {\"city\": \"Seattle\", \"temperature\": 65, \"condition\": \"Cloudy\"},\n",
    "    {\"city\": \"Los Angeles\", \"temperature\": 78, \"condition\": \"Sunny\"},\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🚀 Create DataFrames\n",
    "companies_df = session.create_dataframe(companies)\n",
    "weather_df = session.create_dataframe(weather_data)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🏢 Companies DataFrame:\")\n",
    "companies_df.show()\n",
    "print(\"\\n🌡️ Weather DataFrame:\")\n",
    "weather_df.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🔗 Semantic join - matches \"NYC\" with \"New York City\", \"SF Bay Area\" with \"San Francisco\", etc.\n",
    "semantic_joined = companies_df.semantic.join(\n",
    "    weather_df,\n",
    "    left_on=\"location\",\n",
    "    right_on=\"city\",\n",
    "    join_type=\"left\"  # Keep all companies, even without weather data\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n🔗 Semantic Join Results:\")\n",
    "print(\"(Notice how 'NYC' matched with 'New York City' and 'SF Bay Area' with 'San Francisco')\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "semantic_joined.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "summarization-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 📄 Example 5: Core Capability - Text Summarization\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"Distill pages of content into key insights\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Whether it's customer feedback, research papers, or meeting notes, Fenic can summarize any amount of text while preserving the key information. Perfect for processing large documents or creating executive summaries at scale."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "summarization",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📝 Long-form customer feedback (the kind that's hard to process manually)\n",
    "customer_feedback = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"feedback_id\": \"FB001\",\n",
    "        \"content\": \"\"\"I've been using your product for about 6 months now, and overall I'm quite satisfied with the experience. The user interface is intuitive and clean, which was one of the main reasons I chose your solution over competitors. However, I've encountered several issues that I think need attention. First, the mobile app occasionally crashes when I'm trying to sync large files - this happens maybe once or twice a week and it's quite frustrating because I lose my progress. Second, the search functionality could be much better. Sometimes I'm looking for a specific document and it takes forever to find it, even when I know exactly what I'm searching for. The filters help but they're not comprehensive enough. On the positive side, your customer support team has been fantastic. Every time I've reached out, they've been responsive and helpful. The integration with Google Workspace has been seamless and saves me tons of time. I'd definitely recommend this to colleagues, but please fix those mobile issues soon!\"\"\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"feedback_id\": \"FB002\", \n",
    "        \"content\": \"\"\"As a small business owner, I need tools that just work without requiring a technical team to manage them. Your platform delivers on that promise beautifully. The setup was straightforward - took me about 30 minutes to get everything configured, which is impressive given how comprehensive the feature set is. My team adapted quickly because the learning curve is very gentle. What I appreciate most is the reporting dashboard. Being able to see our key metrics at a glance helps me make better business decisions. The export functionality is also crucial for our accounting processes. If I had to suggest improvements, it would be in the area of customization. While the default templates work well, I'd love more flexibility to brand them according to our company guidelines. Also, the pricing tiers jump quite a bit - a middle option would be perfect for businesses like mine that are growing but not quite ready for the enterprise level. That said, the value we're getting is definitely worth the current price point.\"\"\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"feedback_id\": \"FB003\",\n",
    "        \"content\": \"\"\"I work in a highly regulated industry where security and compliance are absolutely critical. Your platform has exceeded our expectations in this regard. The SOC 2 Type II certification gave us confidence, and the detailed audit logs help us meet our compliance requirements effortlessly. The role-based access controls are granular enough for our needs without being overly complex. Our IT team appreciates the SSO integration and the fact that we can enforce MFA across the organization. Performance-wise, everything runs smoothly even with our team of 200+ users. The API documentation is comprehensive and our developers were able to integrate with our existing systems without any major issues. My only concern is around the upcoming price increase announced last quarter. While I understand the need to invest in new features, a 25% increase is significant for our budget planning. We're evaluating alternatives but honestly, the switching costs would be enormous given how embedded your solution is in our workflows.\"\"\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "feedback_df = session.create_dataframe(customer_feedback)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📄 Summarize each piece of feedback into key points\n",
    "summarized_df = feedback_df.select(\n",
    "    \"feedback_id\",\n",
    "    fc.semantic.summarize(\n",
    "        \"content\",\n",
    "        max_output_tokens=150  # Keep summaries concise\n",
    "    ).alias(\"summary\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📄 Feedback Summaries:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "summarized_df.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📊 Extract sentiment for quick insights\n",
    "sentiment_df = feedback_df.select(\n",
    "    \"feedback_id\",\n",
    "    fc.semantic.analyze_sentiment(\"content\").alias(\"sentiment\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n😊 Sentiment Analysis:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 30)\n",
    "sentiment_df.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "mapping-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🔄 Example 6: Core Capability - Content Mapping\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"Transform text with AI-powered transformations\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Sometimes you need to transform content from one format to another - like turning technical documentation into user-friendly explanations, or converting formal emails into casual social media posts. Semantic mapping does this intelligently while preserving the core meaning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "mapping",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 🤖 Technical API documentation (developer-focused)\n",
    "api_docs = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"endpoint\": \"POST /api/users\",\n",
    "        \"description\": \"Creates a new user resource in the system. Requires authentication header with valid Bearer token. Request body must contain 'email' and 'password' fields with email format validation and minimum password length of 8 characters. Returns 201 on success with user object, 400 for validation errors, 409 for duplicate email.\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"endpoint\": \"GET /api/analytics/dashboard\", \n",
    "        \"description\": \"Retrieves aggregated analytics data for dashboard visualization. Supports optional query parameters: 'start_date' (ISO 8601 format), 'end_date' (ISO 8601 format), 'metrics' (comma-separated list: views,clicks,conversions). Returns paginated results with cursor-based pagination. Requires 'analytics:read' permission scope.\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"endpoint\": \"DELETE /api/files/{id}\",\n",
    "        \"description\": \"Permanently removes a file resource from cloud storage. Path parameter 'id' must be valid UUID format. Soft delete implemented with 30-day retention period. Returns 204 No Content on successful deletion, 404 if file not found, 403 if user lacks delete permissions for the resource.\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "docs_df = session.create_dataframe(api_docs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🔄 Transform technical docs into user-friendly explanations\n",
    "user_friendly_df = docs_df.select(\n",
    "    \"endpoint\",\n",
    "    fc.semantic.map(\n",
    "        \"Transform this technical API documentation into a simple, user-friendly explanation that a non-technical person could understand. Focus on what the feature does for the user, not the technical details.\",\n",
    "        content=fc.builtin.col(\"description\"),\n",
    "        model_alias=\"fast\"\n",
    "    ).alias(\"user_friendly_description\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🔄 Technical → User-Friendly Transformation:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "user_friendly_df.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📱 Also transform to social media friendly posts\n",
    "social_posts_df = docs_df.select(\n",
    "    \"endpoint\",\n",
    "    fc.semantic.map(\n",
    "        \"Turn this API documentation into an engaging social media post that highlights the cool feature. Make it exciting and include relevant emojis. Keep it under 280 characters.\",\n",
    "        content=fc.builtin.col(\"description\"),\n",
    "        model_alias=\"fast\"\n",
    "    ).alias(\"social_post\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n📱 Social Media Posts:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 30)\n",
    "social_posts_df.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "templates-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 📝 Example 7: Productivity - Jinja Prompt Templates\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hook:** *\"Prompt engineering that feels like programming\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "Managing complex prompts is hard. Jinja templates let you create reusable, maintainable prompts with variables, loops, and conditions. Perfect for scaling prompt engineering across your team while maintaining consistency and version control."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "templates",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 📝 Define reusable prompt templates with Jinja2\n",
    "email_analysis_template = \"\"\"\n",
    "You are an expert email analyst. Analyze the following email for:\n",
    "\n",
    "{% if include_sentiment %}\n",
    "- Sentiment: positive, negative, or neutral\n",
    "{% endif %}\n",
    "{% if include_urgency %}\n",
    "- Urgency level: {{ urgency_levels | join(', ') }}\n",
    "{% endif %}\n",
    "{% if include_topics %}\n",
    "- Main topics discussed\n",
    "{% endif %}\n",
    "\n",
    "Email content:\n",
    "{{ email_content }}\n",
    "\n",
    "{% if examples and examples|length > 0 %}\n",
    "Here are some examples of similar analysis:\n",
    "{% for example in examples %}\n",
    "Example {{ loop.index }}: {{ example }}\n",
    "{% endfor %}\n",
    "{% endif %}\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📧 Sample customer emails\n",
    "customer_emails = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"email_id\": \"E001\",\n",
    "        \"content\": \"URGENT: Our production system has been down for 2 hours. Customers are unable to access their accounts and we're losing money every minute this continues. Please escalate to your highest priority support team immediately!\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"email_id\": \"E002\", \n",
    "        \"content\": \"Hi there! I just wanted to reach out and say thank you for the amazing customer service last week. Your team went above and beyond to help resolve my billing question. It's rare to find companies that care this much about their customers.\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"email_id\": \"E003\",\n",
    "        \"content\": \"I've been trying to figure out how to export my data from your platform. I checked the documentation but couldn't find clear instructions. Could someone point me in the right direction? No rush, just whenever someone has a moment.\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "emails_df = session.create_dataframe(customer_emails)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🎛️ Define analysis schema\n",
    "class EmailAnalysis(BaseModel):\n",
    "    sentiment: str = Field(description=\"Overall sentiment of the email\")\n",
    "    urgency: str = Field(description=\"How urgent is this email\")\n",
    "    main_topics: List[str] = Field(description=\"Key topics discussed\")\n",
    "    requires_immediate_response: bool = Field(description=\"Does this need immediate attention\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 🔄 Use Jinja template in semantic operations\n",
    "analyzed_emails = emails_df.select(\n",
    "    \"email_id\",\n",
    "    fc.semantic.extract(\n",
    "        fc.semantic.map(\n",
    "            email_analysis_template,\n",
    "            email_content=fc.builtin.col(\"content\"),\n",
    "            include_sentiment=True,\n",
    "            include_urgency=True, \n",
    "            include_topics=True,\n",
    "            urgency_levels=[\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"critical\"],\n",
    "            examples=[\"Positive feedback: sentiment=positive, urgency=low\", \"Bug report: sentiment=negative, urgency=high\"]\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        EmailAnalysis,\n",
    "        model_alias=\"fast\"\n",
    "    ).alias(\"analysis\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 📊 Display results with structured extraction\n",
    "results_df = analyzed_emails.select(\n",
    "    \"email_id\",\n",
    "    analyzed_emails.analysis.sentiment.alias(\"sentiment\"),\n",
    "    analyzed_emails.analysis.urgency.alias(\"urgency\"),\n",
    "    analyzed_emails.analysis.main_topics.alias(\"topics\"),\n",
